WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.800
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:14.070 --> 00:18.020
"Log.0" is a very important project.

3
00:19.080 --> 00:22.150
Kyoichi. Can I count on you to supervise it?

4
00:22.150 --> 00:24.150
Of course, Father.

5
00:24.150 --> 00:26.590
I will see it through to its end.

6
00:33.200 --> 00:35.050
He really looks just like him.

7
00:36.290 --> 00:38.080
Like an exact copy.

8
00:45.850 --> 00:47.710
My name is Ushio.

9
00:55.940 --> 00:58.000
It's an honor to meet you.

10
01:08.980 --> 01:10.820
You called?

11
01:10.820 --> 01:12.460
Yes.

12
01:12.460 --> 01:14.960
I wanted to talk in person. Alone.

13
01:14.960 --> 01:18.460
I'm glad you're ready. Let's agree on where to meet.

14
01:18.460 --> 01:20.260
Alright.

15
01:20.260 --> 01:22.770
Will you come to Yamashiro Art Museum?

16
01:24.040 --> 01:26.010
That's where Shiharu is.

17
01:38.350 --> 01:44.750
[I will be transporting the Roopkund girl to Nichie's Applied Tech Center]

18
01:55.660 --> 01:59.220
Please leave a message after the tone.

19
02:00.330 --> 02:03.190
If you saw the email I sent earlier...

20
02:03.190 --> 02:06.060
Canceled? All of his plans?

21
02:06.060 --> 02:09.440
Yes. I had assumed you knew.

22
02:09.440 --> 02:11.450
No, I wasn't informed.

23
02:13.980 --> 02:16.000
Thank you for filling me in.

24
02:23.190 --> 02:25.620
What is he planning?

25
02:41.230 --> 02:45.840
[log.9]

26
02:48.530 --> 02:50.230
You bastards are falling for it!

27
02:50.230 --> 02:52.390
Please return to your room.

28
02:56.170 --> 03:00.470
I was set up! It's all a trick!

29
03:14.120 --> 03:18.980
- Grandma, look! Bubbles! - Oh my!

30
03:18.980 --> 03:21.080
Very beautiful.

31
03:21.980 --> 03:24.230
Ubongo!

32
03:39.080 --> 03:40.980
Good afternoon, sir.

33
03:44.230 --> 03:46.100
You...

34
03:48.080 --> 03:49.920
You set me up.

35
03:49.920 --> 03:51.230
Yes.

36
03:51.850 --> 03:57.910
I had a informant falsely testify you were selling him information.

37
03:59.060 --> 04:01.070
But not to worry.

38
04:01.070 --> 04:04.850
Once this matter is settled, you will be proved innocent.

39
04:08.190 --> 04:11.490
So everything is going as Plantae planned?

40
04:11.490 --> 04:17.420
Of course. We have successfully halted this investigation.

41
04:18.370 --> 04:24.210
You'd be able to erase all our security footage.

42
04:24.210 --> 04:26.370
Yes, I could.

43
04:26.370 --> 04:28.340
I was in charge of them, after all.

44
04:30.490 --> 04:35.970
And when those bones were stolen from Ishimizaki's lab...

45
04:42.690 --> 04:46.420
Plantae has believers everywhere.

46
04:47.450 --> 04:50.080
All is connected in this world.

47
04:51.750 --> 04:55.250
Do you get it now, Tada?

48
04:57.540 --> 05:00.380
Please, do not misunderstand.

49
05:00.920 --> 05:04.850
We only wish to save the girl.

50
05:04.850 --> 05:07.370
An organization protects the individual.

51
05:07.370 --> 05:11.830
That is the sort of helping hand we at Plantae hope to offer.

52
05:11.830 --> 05:14.340
All manners occur in an eternal cycle.

53
05:14.340 --> 05:18.930
Our actions will one day aid you as well.

54
05:23.560 --> 05:26.370
As if I believe that.

55
05:27.540 --> 05:33.870
You people are just following orders.

56
05:33.870 --> 05:40.000
You're obeying a clone of your own making!

57
05:42.620 --> 05:46.450
It's so society can live in peace and harmony.

58
05:50.550 --> 05:52.760
- The documents. - Thanks.

59
06:01.210 --> 06:03.750
[Findings at Lake Roopkund] [Cloning technology]

60
06:03.750 --> 06:05.590
[Nichie Pharmaceutical]

61
06:28.500 --> 06:31.190
[In order to protect her own identity...]

62
06:31.190 --> 06:34.750
I just want to see Shiharu, one last time.

63
06:36.700 --> 06:39.360
[...she ordered the deaths of others.]

64
07:02.150 --> 07:06.020
I have plenty of memories in Nichie City.

65
07:21.310 --> 07:26.150
On my way home, I'd always think about how Shiharu would be waiting for me.

66
07:29.460 --> 07:33.050
So you always waited for Haruka?

67
07:34.410 --> 07:35.850
Yeah.

68
07:36.690 --> 07:39.510
I'd kill time by reading a book.

69
07:40.700 --> 07:43.160
No wonder you're so smart.

70
07:44.500 --> 07:46.750
I definitely read a lot.

71
07:47.630 --> 07:50.610
I usually started our conversations.

72
07:50.610 --> 07:54.490
Shiharu would be too absorbed in a book.

73
07:54.490 --> 07:58.390
The truth is, I always noticed.

74
07:59.950 --> 08:02.910
But I wanted to hear him say my name.

75
08:05.290 --> 08:09.160
So he never managed to catch you off guard?

76
08:13.110 --> 08:18.090
I wasn't even reading on that bench.

77
08:18.860 --> 08:23.170
I was just waiting for him to come home.

78
08:34.590 --> 08:36.390
That's so cute.

79
08:38.610 --> 08:42.830
I couldn't do much else.

80
08:56.250 --> 08:59.280
I'd love to take you there one day.

81
09:00.220 --> 09:02.710
It really was a beautiful place.

82
09:49.980 --> 09:57.920
[The truth from 27 years ago] [Unraveling all the mysteries]

83
10:01.150 --> 10:02.960
You're late.

84
10:02.960 --> 10:04.560
I'm home.

85
10:05.520 --> 10:08.580
We're going to the museum tonight, right?

86
10:08.580 --> 10:10.710
Oh, right...

87
10:10.710 --> 10:14.230
Sorry, maybe not today. I'm a bit tired.

88
10:15.450 --> 10:19.140
I spent the entire day doing thesis research in the library.

89
10:20.090 --> 10:22.790
You've been really busy with your thesis.

90
10:24.000 --> 10:27.060
Yeah. I figured I'd try for a PhD.

91
10:27.060 --> 10:30.050
It could be useful in the future.

92
10:31.450 --> 10:35.230
Is genetics that interesting?

93
10:35.230 --> 10:37.900
You're always reading about it.

94
10:37.900 --> 10:40.370
I was inspired.

95
10:42.110 --> 10:43.990
That's not why I read.

96
10:43.990 --> 10:45.810
Huh?

97
10:45.810 --> 10:48.430
The two of us read

98
10:49.610 --> 10:52.250
for very different reasons.

99
10:54.320 --> 10:56.200
What do you mean?

100
11:14.880 --> 11:20.030
[Incoming typhoon]

101
11:46.830 --> 11:48.720
Sir, where are you going?

102
11:48.720 --> 11:50.490
I have private matters to attend to.

103
11:50.490 --> 11:51.930
Have you managed to contact your son?

104
11:51.930 --> 11:55.040
I will deal with him myself.

105
11:56.070 --> 11:58.410
Was he able to see his sister?

106
11:59.260 --> 12:01.720
The clone from "log.0" is alive.

107
12:02.290 --> 12:03.760
Am I correct?

108
12:10.040 --> 12:15.850
I have the files here to prove your illegal use of Nichie funding.

109
12:15.850 --> 12:20.840
Was this money used to keep the clone alive?

110
12:23.210 --> 12:26.870
You're not desperate to bury a mistake left by your predecessor.

111
12:26.870 --> 12:29.640
You wish to hide your own mess.

112
12:30.540 --> 12:32.600
Why?

113
12:32.600 --> 12:34.510
Is it all for Plantae?

114
12:35.770 --> 12:37.200
We'll talk tomorrow.

115
12:37.200 --> 12:39.380
We have to talk, now.

116
12:41.190 --> 12:43.300
Otherwise, I...

117
12:44.610 --> 12:47.350
Can't trust your own judgement?

118
12:50.250 --> 12:51.830
Sir.

119
12:54.590 --> 12:57.750
I always thought of you as a father.

120
12:57.750 --> 12:59.560
That is precisely

121
13:00.730 --> 13:03.510
the sort of burden I never wanted to become.

122
13:11.020 --> 13:14.880
[Nichie Pharmaceutical]

123
13:14.880 --> 13:19.360
[Nichie Pharmaceutical Applied Tech Center]

124
14:24.070 --> 14:25.870
Gather anyone who's available.

125
14:25.870 --> 14:27.220
Yes, ma'am.

126
14:29.910 --> 14:32.750
Mayuzumi? This is Kasuga.

127
14:32.750 --> 14:35.370
Is everything alright?

128
14:37.910 --> 14:40.230
What? Our Mataji? [T/N: Indian honorific meaning "Holy Mother"]

129
14:54.920 --> 14:57.700
- Haruka? - Stay back!

130
14:57.700 --> 14:59.070
What are you doing here?

131
14:59.070 --> 15:01.310
I told you Shiharu was at the museum!

132
15:01.310 --> 15:04.730
The man named Kojima was killed by Ushio.

133
15:04.730 --> 15:07.130
You gave the order, didn't you?

134
15:08.320 --> 15:10.120
Didn't you?

135
15:12.020 --> 15:14.080
Ushio will be arriving shortly.

136
15:14.080 --> 15:15.320
You have to go.

137
15:15.320 --> 15:18.050
As if I'd believe a word you say!

138
15:18.050 --> 15:19.640
I'm telling the truth!

139
15:20.490 --> 15:22.890
I plan to put an end to everything today.

140
15:22.890 --> 15:27.460
I came here to kill Ushio.

141
15:27.460 --> 15:28.980
Why?

142
15:28.980 --> 15:33.320
Haruka. I'll keep no more secrets from you.

143
15:33.320 --> 15:35.200
What are you referring to?

144
15:35.960 --> 15:41.430
The part where you created Shiharu? The fact that you used my mother?

145
15:43.540 --> 15:45.000
Tell me everything.

146
15:47.160 --> 15:48.750
You're right.

147
15:51.040 --> 15:56.160
It all began right here, in this very institute.

148
16:00.460 --> 16:02.390
But Kaede...

149
16:03.910 --> 16:05.830
Your mother...

150
16:07.330 --> 16:09.950
She chose to participate in the project.

151
16:14.730 --> 16:17.390
- As if. - It's true.

152
16:20.440 --> 16:25.000
She willingly volunteered of her own accord.

153
16:36.270 --> 16:41.040
These are the five candidates who will birth our Holy Woman, our Mataji.

154
16:41.040 --> 16:42.680
Please, come on in.

155
16:56.370 --> 17:00.510
These are the doctors who will oversee the operation.

156
17:14.570 --> 17:18.400
Everything will be okay, Haruka.

157
17:18.900 --> 17:22.560
Mommy will be a bit busy.

158
17:23.250 --> 17:28.220
But my fellow members will take great care of you, okay?

159
17:38.520 --> 17:42.420
I didn't think I'd find you at Plantae.

160
17:45.780 --> 17:50.530
When my son's father passed away,

161
17:50.530 --> 17:53.550
my fellow members helped raise him.

162
17:55.640 --> 17:58.580
Without the teachings of Brother Manabe,

163
17:59.280 --> 18:04.680
my son and I would have been very lost.

164
18:08.370 --> 18:15.220
That's why I feel honored to have been chosen.

165
18:16.910 --> 18:18.430
I see.

166
18:20.980 --> 18:24.340
Did you realize who I was right away?

167
18:25.870 --> 18:29.170
Of course. You haven't changed one bit.

168
18:30.980 --> 18:34.340
She and I were childhood friends.

169
18:34.340 --> 18:37.690
She's a very smart individual. Always has been.

170
18:37.690 --> 18:41.480
I remember she wanted to become a teacher.

171
18:41.480 --> 18:44.900
What a coincidence to reunite here.

172
18:44.900 --> 18:46.940
Don't tell the other staff about this.

173
18:46.940 --> 18:50.190
I wouldn't want them to think I'm playing favorites.

174
18:50.190 --> 18:53.660
I won't treat her any differently either.

175
18:53.660 --> 18:55.440
This project's success is our priority.

176
18:55.440 --> 18:56.660
Indeed.

177
18:56.660 --> 19:00.990
Your father needs to see how capable you really are.

178
19:00.990 --> 19:04.770
My father has nothing to do with this.

179
19:04.770 --> 19:07.130
Right. Sorry about that.

180
19:07.670 --> 19:10.690
[Transplanted cells]

181
19:10.690 --> 19:15.590
All transplanted clone embryo look as intended.

182
19:16.240 --> 19:20.520
Then everything is going smoothly thus far.

183
19:20.520 --> 19:24.000
Now we simply monitor the health of each mother.

184
19:24.610 --> 19:26.620
We leave them in your care.

185
19:38.980 --> 19:44.020
We will have you both take a shot of progestogen.

186
19:44.650 --> 19:46.330
What?

187
19:46.330 --> 19:50.820
They will help stabilize your fluctuating hormones.

188
20:21.770 --> 20:24.410
Let's see what our results are.

189
20:32.600 --> 20:35.560
Just one?

190
20:35.560 --> 20:39.450
Even one success is something to celebrate.

191
20:39.450 --> 20:42.550
Can you supplement us with extra mothers?

192
20:43.110 --> 20:47.100
One mother will suffice for our Mataji.

193
21:04.200 --> 21:06.410
How do you feel?

194
21:06.410 --> 21:07.920
Much better.

195
21:07.920 --> 21:09.430
Really?

196
21:11.240 --> 21:13.080
That's good to hear.

197
21:15.240 --> 21:17.140
I brought you a little something.

198
21:17.790 --> 21:19.180
Here.

199
21:22.300 --> 21:24.770
Do you still like chestnut yokan? [T/N: a type of Japanese dessert]

200
21:26.480 --> 21:28.960
Pregnant women need their sugar.

201
21:28.960 --> 21:30.780
Maybe that's generalizing things.

202
21:30.780 --> 21:34.060
Sorry, this is all a first for me.

203
21:34.720 --> 21:38.020
I'm only allowed to eat certain things...

204
21:38.020 --> 21:41.350
Don't worry about that. I run this place.

205
21:44.560 --> 21:46.220
Thank you.

206
21:47.340 --> 21:50.680
You remembered my favorites?

207
21:51.450 --> 21:54.060
How could I not, when you'd steal my share?

208
21:54.060 --> 21:56.800
Never underestimate a grudge over food.

209
21:58.450 --> 22:00.340
What? If someone finds out...

210
22:00.340 --> 22:01.740
It's just a small snack.

211
22:01.740 --> 22:04.020
You said you wouldn't play favorites.

212
22:04.020 --> 22:06.810
It's my job to look after the mother.

213
22:07.510 --> 22:09.520
She's with those people.

214
22:09.520 --> 22:11.940
Stray too close, and you'll never return to normalcy.

215
22:11.940 --> 22:15.010
We've strayed far off the path already.

216
22:19.100 --> 22:20.930
Sorry.

217
22:21.540 --> 22:23.550
I'm in no position to criticize.

218
22:30.460 --> 22:32.830
I see Dr. Senba has yet to arrive.

219
22:37.520 --> 22:39.200
How goes the project?

220
22:39.200 --> 22:41.260
It's been running smoothly.

221
23:07.060 --> 23:10.090
Our team of specialists will care for our Mataji

222
23:10.090 --> 23:14.490
after you give birth to her.

223
23:14.490 --> 23:19.690
Would you please supply us with feeding milk?

224
23:20.730 --> 23:24.360
I won't be breastfeeding her directly?

225
23:24.360 --> 23:30.750
Our Mataji cannot grow attached to one individual, even her mother.

226
23:31.540 --> 23:35.640
These are the teachings Brother Manabe left us.

227
23:49.960 --> 23:51.730
What're you doing out here?

228
23:51.730 --> 23:53.350
Oh, well...

229
23:55.740 --> 23:57.420
What?

230
24:01.520 --> 24:04.070
Since I haven't gone home in a while...

231
24:04.070 --> 24:05.830
Ah, your daughter.

232
24:06.990 --> 24:08.730
What did you say her name was?

233
24:08.730 --> 24:10.150
Mari.

234
24:10.150 --> 24:13.000
Written with the character to mean "truth".

235
24:15.110 --> 24:16.970
A fitting name coming from you.

236
24:30.160 --> 24:31.970
She just moved.

237
24:34.940 --> 24:37.220
See? There she goes again.

238
24:43.570 --> 24:46.020
Put your ear to my belly, and listen.

239
25:00.020 --> 25:02.040
Shiharu.

240
25:02.040 --> 25:03.350
Huh?

241
25:05.310 --> 25:07.240
"Shiharu"?

242
25:07.240 --> 25:08.690
Yes.

243
25:08.690 --> 25:13.350
Do you remember the art museum

244
25:13.350 --> 25:16.560
we used to walk by in high school?

245
25:16.560 --> 25:18.780
Of course I do.

246
25:18.780 --> 25:23.790
Whenever I thought of you, I'd think back to those stone steps.

247
25:24.410 --> 25:28.980
There were beautiful hydrangeas blooming whenever we visited.

248
25:30.370 --> 25:32.140
Hydrangeas... [T/N: "Shiharu" can also mean hydrangeas]

249
25:36.860 --> 25:39.580
Our Mataji will be safely born, yes?

250
25:39.580 --> 25:43.770
Oh shut up and pray to a god, why don't you.

251
25:43.770 --> 25:47.350
No... Have you failed?

252
25:47.350 --> 25:51.190
- What? - Dr. Senba cannot predict every outcome.

253
25:51.190 --> 25:53.200
This was well within my predictions.

254
25:53.200 --> 25:56.600
The donor's DNA was already damaged,

255
25:56.600 --> 26:01.160
and there was always a risk of transferring said DNA to an egg cell.

256
26:01.160 --> 26:04.760
Yes, but no one can ever predict the end result.

257
26:04.760 --> 26:06.500
Perhaps you can't.

258
26:06.500 --> 26:08.660
Then this will be a success?

259
26:11.330 --> 26:14.050
I'm doing everything perfectly.

260
26:14.050 --> 26:15.360
Will it be a success?

261
26:15.360 --> 26:19.550
If you're so worried, you should've prepared extra mothers like I asked.

262
26:19.550 --> 26:21.330
I will, for the next time.

263
26:21.330 --> 26:24.680
We will continue until we find success, yes?

264
26:25.950 --> 26:30.410
Your Holy Woman is marked by success or failure?

265
26:32.040 --> 26:34.730
You are dealing with the fate of a human being.

266
26:34.730 --> 26:38.450
There is no "next time" for the life in her stomach!

267
26:40.360 --> 26:42.530
Don't mind him.

268
26:42.530 --> 26:46.430
No reason to try and preach morals now.

269
26:47.590 --> 26:50.460
Morals are entirely necessary in our work.

270
26:52.320 --> 26:55.010
We are creating a living person.

271
26:55.580 --> 26:57.770
"We"?

272
26:58.370 --> 27:01.640
I'm the one doing the creating.

273
27:05.400 --> 27:13.040
This blade is to be bestowed on our Mataji.

274
27:15.460 --> 27:18.010
I want you to hold onto it.

275
27:18.850 --> 27:23.890
We can only pray to Brother Manabe now.

276
27:43.860 --> 27:45.650
Have I failed?

277
27:49.240 --> 27:52.300
Will this child die in my stomach?

278
28:00.810 --> 28:03.520
We're simply taking precautions.

279
28:03.520 --> 28:07.710
Don't worry. Your child will...

280
28:09.660 --> 28:13.600
The Mataji will be born into this world.

281
28:14.950 --> 28:16.690
She's mine.

282
28:19.500 --> 28:22.260
My baby.

283
28:28.830 --> 28:30.620
You're right.

284
28:31.190 --> 28:32.910
She's your child.

285
28:34.870 --> 28:36.670
She's your Shiharu.

286
28:38.650 --> 28:40.480
Shiharu...

287
28:41.660 --> 28:43.560
A short while afterwards,

288
28:43.560 --> 28:48.680
my father and lead of "log.0", Yumihiko Nanase, died.

289
28:50.270 --> 28:54.980
With the loss of protection that Yumihiko's influence gave us,

290
28:54.980 --> 28:57.640
the team had no choice but to disband.

291
28:58.520 --> 29:01.580
However...

292
29:05.370 --> 29:06.950
Steady, you can do this.

293
29:06.950 --> 29:09.680
This has nothing to do with the project...

294
29:10.280 --> 29:12.460
Right?

295
29:12.460 --> 29:15.850
That's right.

296
29:18.250 --> 29:23.760
I will always be here for you, and your child.

297
29:24.790 --> 29:26.740
Always.

298
29:50.270 --> 29:53.830
I told my fellow researchers it was a stillbirth.

299
29:55.730 --> 29:58.140
Only Ishimizaki knew the truth.

300
30:00.310 --> 30:03.360
Was this what Kaede wanted?

301
30:03.360 --> 30:04.890
I wanted this as well.

302
30:06.560 --> 30:10.040
I thought it was the right choice.

303
30:12.360 --> 30:15.590
You've prioritized your love for her over Plantae,

304
30:15.590 --> 30:18.420
and your own company.

305
30:33.120 --> 30:35.430
You'll be walking a thorny path.

306
30:45.460 --> 30:51.380
Shiharu couldn't survive without an incubator.

307
30:54.500 --> 30:59.210
This facility's sole purpose was to keep her alive.

308
31:00.340 --> 31:07.180
In order to keep Shiharu a secret, Kaede remained loyal to Plantae.

309
31:10.360 --> 31:13.350
Shiharu was eventually able to leave this place,

310
31:13.350 --> 31:16.680
but you know the story from there.

311
32:10.340 --> 32:13.180
Another all-nighter?

312
32:17.410 --> 32:19.960
You sure do work hard.

313
32:21.850 --> 32:23.890
Onodera.

314
32:24.830 --> 32:30.720
Why are we doing all this?

315
32:36.810 --> 32:39.260
Isn't that obvious?

316
32:41.400 --> 32:46.000
It's so society can live in peace and harmony.

317
32:52.040 --> 32:55.370
That's not something I'd expect you to say.

318
32:56.560 --> 32:59.470
Something you can never hope to achieve, sir.

319
33:00.690 --> 33:02.630
Hey, watch your mouth...

320
33:21.820 --> 33:26.470
Why would you send us this evidence?

321
33:29.420 --> 33:33.040
I figured you people would appreciate it,

322
33:33.040 --> 33:36.060
as the individuals in direct opposition to our current leader.

323
33:41.140 --> 33:46.640
Let us put an end to Kyoichi Nanase.

324
33:48.360 --> 33:54.910
Are you not working with Nanase to drag us all under?

325
33:57.370 --> 33:59.840
Please make your choice.

326
34:01.490 --> 34:04.000
You expect us to believe you?

327
34:04.000 --> 34:07.460
We know you owe a great deal to Nanase.

328
34:08.120 --> 34:10.820
A great deal is an understatement.

329
34:10.820 --> 34:13.930
- Then... - This is my way of repaying the favor.

330
34:15.120 --> 34:16.790
What?

331
34:18.350 --> 34:20.290
That man...

332
34:21.210 --> 34:26.500
He wants to part ways with his baggage.

333
34:29.520 --> 34:31.290
I remember...

334
34:32.340 --> 34:34.800
We used to be so happy together.

335
34:37.150 --> 34:39.150
- Haruka! - Yeah?

336
34:39.150 --> 34:41.790
Can you help Shiharu?

337
34:41.790 --> 34:43.180
Sure.

338
34:44.590 --> 34:45.710
- Are you okay? - Yeah.

339
34:45.710 --> 34:47.440
- I'll get it. - Thanks.

340
34:47.440 --> 34:48.650
Sure.

341
34:48.650 --> 34:50.170
What's for dinner?

342
34:50.170 --> 34:52.030
Okonomiyaki. [T/N: Savory pancakes]

343
34:52.030 --> 34:53.580
Can you grab the fishcake from the fridge?

344
34:53.580 --> 34:54.770
- Sure. - Where's this going?

345
34:54.770 --> 34:56.730
- The living room. - Okay.

346
34:56.730 --> 34:59.860
- Should I get those? - Yes, thank you.

347
34:59.860 --> 35:02.340
Can't have okonomiyaki without fishcake.

348
35:02.340 --> 35:04.060
Exactly.

349
35:04.060 --> 35:05.680
- Thanks. - Can you chop them?

350
35:05.680 --> 35:07.380
Sure thing.

351
35:11.900 --> 35:15.930
- Is that on? - I think so.

352
35:25.830 --> 35:28.920
- See? It's warm. - Yup. Definitely on.

353
35:39.850 --> 35:45.410
You were the reason I could see Shiharu smile.

354
35:51.440 --> 35:53.350
What are you talking about?

355
35:58.200 --> 36:00.170
"Happy together"?

356
36:03.420 --> 36:06.180
You murdered my mother.

357
36:08.950 --> 36:12.800
She died because she gave birth to a clone.

358
36:12.800 --> 36:17.910
That's right. Kaede's body paid the price in the years to come.

359
36:18.530 --> 36:23.740
Her deteriorating health is why Ishimizaki felt guilt.

360
36:23.740 --> 36:29.250
His breaking point was seeing how weak Shiharu had become.

361
36:30.410 --> 36:32.700
We must atone for our sins

362
36:32.700 --> 36:35.330
by going public with our knowledge, and...

363
36:35.330 --> 36:37.700
Please, reconsider.

364
36:37.700 --> 36:40.070
We've worked together this long.

365
36:40.070 --> 36:43.690
If we release everything to the world, our careers are over.

366
36:43.690 --> 36:47.690
Our actions deserve backlash.

367
36:47.690 --> 36:49.350
We've committed a human taboo.

368
36:49.350 --> 36:51.800
Think about Shiharu.

369
36:52.360 --> 36:56.320
She can't survive without Nichie's facilities.

370
36:56.320 --> 36:59.040
She doesn't have long.

371
37:00.490 --> 37:04.080
If we make our findings known and garner public sympathy,

372
37:04.080 --> 37:06.240
she could receive care using the latest technology.

373
37:06.240 --> 37:08.450
We're developing medicines of our own.

374
37:08.450 --> 37:11.370
- Give it a bit more... - Kyoichi, you should know!

375
37:11.370 --> 37:14.740
- She has no time! - Shiharu doesn't want to be a spectacle.

376
37:14.740 --> 37:17.680
She doesn't want to die, either!

377
37:21.120 --> 37:23.920
Ishimizaki's mind was set.

378
37:23.920 --> 37:25.860
He had you analyze the skeleton, and...

379
37:25.860 --> 37:28.870
You ordered Ushio to kill him!

380
37:28.870 --> 37:30.850
No!

381
37:30.850 --> 37:35.900
No one knows who Ushio obeys now.

382
37:35.900 --> 37:37.790
- Not even Plantae can control him. - Lies!

383
37:37.790 --> 37:39.970
You had him killed!

384
37:41.190 --> 37:43.390
I backed Ishimizaki into a corner.

385
37:44.120 --> 37:46.010
That much I will admit.

386
37:46.710 --> 37:48.250
But...

387
37:49.460 --> 37:52.560
I would never wish for his death.

388
37:54.900 --> 38:01.230
My priority over my company, over being a father,

389
38:01.230 --> 38:07.370
and over Plantae, is keeping Shiharu protected and hidden.

390
38:10.730 --> 38:13.390
What a selfish excuse.

391
38:15.610 --> 38:18.840
Professor Ishimizaki, and my mother...

392
38:20.540 --> 38:22.980
They were both murdered because of you, Kayoko Senba,

393
38:24.040 --> 38:27.310
and Plantae's selfish goals.

394
38:30.690 --> 38:33.270
As if any of this is for Shiharu's sake.

395
38:36.330 --> 38:38.020
You...

396
38:40.500 --> 38:42.810
You people!

397
38:46.100 --> 38:47.850
All of you are just...

398
38:51.270 --> 38:55.010
Just toying around with Shiharu's life.

399
38:57.940 --> 38:59.960
You must understand.

400
38:59.960 --> 39:01.810
I care for Shiharu, just as much as you...

401
39:01.810 --> 39:04.010
Shut up!

402
39:05.080 --> 39:09.010
Then why did you take her away?

403
39:10.240 --> 39:13.800
Why did you lie, and tell me she died?

404
39:19.800 --> 39:23.950
You're just making convenient excuses.

405
39:49.520 --> 39:51.160
Why are you...

406
39:52.750 --> 39:55.520
What did you plan to use that for?

407
39:55.520 --> 39:58.130
I will put an end to everything today.

408
39:58.130 --> 39:59.950
Everything.

409
39:59.950 --> 40:02.470
You wanted to kill Ushio?

410
40:02.470 --> 40:04.750
Well, he won't be coming.

411
40:07.690 --> 40:10.190
What?

412
40:10.190 --> 40:14.410
I also came here to put an end to things.

413
40:14.410 --> 40:19.000
I knew you were luring Ushio here.

414
40:22.650 --> 40:25.640
You used me, didn't you?

415
40:26.400 --> 40:30.220
Yes. I did.

416
40:30.900 --> 40:35.560
I knew Ushio was tailing you these past few years.

417
40:36.770 --> 40:43.620
All so I wouldn't tell a soul about our research.

418
40:48.940 --> 40:53.030
[Unknown: Haruka Nanase entered your home] [Someone is tailing you as well]

419
40:59.100 --> 41:01.310
Please stop this.

420
41:01.310 --> 41:04.960
I already know Nanase's boy is at my place.

421
41:04.960 --> 41:07.600
He wasn't just observing my every action.

422
41:07.600 --> 41:11.680
He was tracking my texts, my emails, everything.

423
41:13.100 --> 41:16.500
That was when you sent me an email.

424
41:18.000 --> 41:20.310
[I will be transporting the Roopkund girl to Nichie's Applied Tech Center]

425
41:20.310 --> 41:25.830
You knew Ushio would chase after the Roopkund girl.

426
41:26.770 --> 41:31.520
If you saw the email I sent earlier, please ignore it. There was a mistake.

427
41:31.520 --> 41:35.620
I will convey the correct information to Dr. Senba at a later time.

428
41:38.830 --> 41:43.500
You sent a similar message to me yesterday.

429
41:56.860 --> 41:59.650
[The Roopkund girl is in a building rented out by Nichie Pharmaceutical]

430
41:59.650 --> 42:05.020
I heard a man was found there, dead.

431
42:06.690 --> 42:09.920
You used Ushio to kill that man.

432
42:11.660 --> 42:15.390
It was a test run to see if your plan today would work.

433
42:17.450 --> 42:20.060
You had no other choice.

434
42:20.060 --> 42:23.770
You didn't know who Ushio was obeying.

435
42:23.770 --> 42:25.760
And you do?

436
42:30.530 --> 42:33.440
Of course. The answer is a simple one.

437
42:35.400 --> 42:41.230
That man is taking action for Plantae. For the original Manabe.

438
42:41.230 --> 42:43.460
He isn't following anyone's orders.

439
42:44.190 --> 42:46.960
He's acting on his own self accord.

440
42:47.910 --> 42:52.180
He wants to erase all evidence that lead back to Roopkund.

441
42:52.950 --> 42:54.720
Everything?

442
42:56.120 --> 43:00.060
Ushio is searching for the Roopkund girl

443
43:00.060 --> 43:02.820
so he can get rid of her, for good.

444
43:02.820 --> 43:07.230
What did you do to Ushio?

445
43:08.160 --> 43:11.150
Someone contacted Plantae.

446
43:11.150 --> 43:14.830
A girl with a weak voice, pleading for help.

447
43:14.830 --> 43:17.630
It was the Roopkund girl.

448
43:18.750 --> 43:20.970
Shiharu called them?

449
43:20.970 --> 43:22.510
That's right.

450
43:22.510 --> 43:24.490
What? Our Mataji?

451
43:24.490 --> 43:27.360
Plantae asked me to help.

452
43:27.360 --> 43:34.390
So I used your trick to send Ushio to the Yamashiro Art Museum.

453
43:35.250 --> 43:36.930
Why?

454
43:39.620 --> 43:43.170
Because that's where the Roopkund girl is.

455
43:55.830 --> 43:57.460
Shiharu!

456
44:02.700 --> 44:05.680
This is because you took him from me.

457
44:08.940 --> 44:11.770
Know the pain of having your loved one

458
44:12.880 --> 44:14.980
taken from you.

459
44:25.950 --> 44:30.060
[Yamashiro Art Museum]

460
44:52.750 --> 44:54.550
Wait!

461
44:56.070 --> 44:58.040
No one else is here except me.
